PKGBUILD_RESULT(3)

# NAME

pkgbuild_result - seal complete native build outcomes

# DESCRIPTION

*build_result::succeeded* requires a sealed request, execution-evidence
identity, complete payload manifest, and sealed artifact. It derives a binding
identity over the request, payload, and exact artifact authority.

*build_result::failed* requires a sealed request, execution-evidence identity,
and failure-evidence identity. Failed results contain no payload, artifact, or
artifact binding.

Public construction cannot represent a partial result. Changing source
snapshot, inputs, profiles, architectures, policy, payload, artifact bytes, or
execution evidence changes the build-result identity.

A successful result states intended payload and exact artifact bytes. It does
not by itself prove that an archive decodes to that payload; the verified
planner adapter performs that comparison.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgbuild*(3), *pkgbuild_request*(3), *pkgbuild_plan_adapter*(3)
